<article class="env-lemma" id="0GLL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GLL">Lemma <span data-tag="0GLL">4.24.7</span>.</a> Let $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ be a left adjoint to the functor $v : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}$. Let $\eta _ X : X \to v(u(X))$ be the unit and $\epsilon _ Y : u(v(Y)) \to Y$ be the counit. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  u(X) \xrightarrow {u(\eta _ X)} u(v(u(X)) \xrightarrow {\epsilon _{u(X)}} u(X) \quad \text{and}\quad v(Y) \xrightarrow {\eta _{v(Y)}} v(u(v(Y))) \xrightarrow {v(\epsilon _ Y)} v(Y)  \]
</div>
  <p> are the identity morphisms. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
